From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 08:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: mp01: Run the e-paper I2C at 400 kHz

The e-paper controller's slave I2C port is rated to 400 kHz at most
(Pango UG030004 v1.7, slave I2C section). The board DT took the vendor's
1 MHz, a likely cause of the controller's occasional NAK at 0x4b and of
the stock kernel reading its firmware version as 0. Run the bus within
the rating.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6789-minimal-mp01.dts | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6789-minimal-mp01.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6789-minimal-mp01.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6789-minimal-mp01.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6789-minimal-mp01.dts
@@ -836,11 +836,11 @@
 /*
  * The panel module: a Pango controller that takes the DSI video and drives
- * the e-paper, controlled over I2C at its factory 1 MHz. It registers its
+ * the e-paper, controlled over I2C at its rated 400 kHz. It registers its
  * DSI device on the host its port leads to.
  */
 &i2c7 {
-	clock-frequency = <1000000>;
+	clock-frequency = <400000>;
 	status = "okay";
 
 	display@4b {
 		compatible = "minimal,z10-eink";
-- 
2.47.0
